<p>Baseball now has to compete for attention in a much different TV market than it did in the 1970s. There are more streaming platforms, social media, and channels that have changed how fans watch their favorite team. These changes help explain why world series television viewership. Despite the changing sport of baseball and more data tracking launch angles and power, the MLB has not found a way to bring its viewership to the titan that it once was. This creates a challenge for baseball, creating more exciting moments doesn’t necessarily mean more viewers watching at home.</p>
